      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>The synaxarion, Sǝnkǝsār in Ethiopia, is a liturgical work containing commemorative notices of persons, events or feasts for each day of the year. The Ethiopic
            Sǝnkǝsār war translated from the Copto-Arabic synaxarion at least twice (<t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4032SenkessarS">Sǝnkǝssār (First Recension A)</t:ref>
            and <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4033Senkessar">Sǝnkǝssār (First Recension B)</t:ref>), each translation depending on a different Arabic Vorlage. The translation was extensively revised in Ethiopia, 
            both regarding content and language (<t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4968SenkessarSec">Sǝnkǝssār (General record for the "Second
          Recension")</t:ref>).</t:p>
         </t:abstract>
         <t:creation notBefore="1375" notAfter="1425" corresp="#Psttanthony">The translation  <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4032SenkessarS">Sǝnkǝssār (First Recension A)</t:ref> was carried out around
               <t:date>1400</t:date> by <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8743Semon">Sǝmʿon</t:persName>, a monk of <t:placeName xml:id="Psttanthony" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0320DAA">Monastery of Saint Anthony</t:placeName>, according to the colophon
            of the translation present in <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/BNFabb66A">Paris, Bibliothèque nationale de France, BnF Éthiopien d'Abbadie 66 A</t:ref>.</t:creation>
         <t:creation notBefore="1375" notAfter="1400">The translation <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4033Senkessar">Sǝnkǝssār (First Recension B)</t:ref> goes probably also back to the end of the 14th
            century.</t:creation>
    
